\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 [Prolog] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 >F<Ecit deus ... [Gn 1,16] Per hec duo luminaria}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; (3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 >Prefacio In librum Consonancie Ad Summum pontificem dominum Nicolaum quintum<, {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 >I<N[nachtr\u228 \'e4glich eingef\u252 \'fcgt: ter ce]tera beatissime pater}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; (4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) [Text] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 >I<N principio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [Io 1,1; Ammonius Alexandrinus: Harmonia evangeliorum, PL 68, Sp. 225-358; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 STEGM\u220 \'dcLLER, RB 2, Nr. 1280}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ]; [Kommentar] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 >I<N principio [Io 1,1]. >Orpheus< uetustissimus poetarum: Deum uerum et magnum}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ... - \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (165\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Schlu\u223 \'df des Textes) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et sermonem confirmante sequentibus signis. >\u182 \'b6< Explicit. deo laudes; ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 - (166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Schlu\u223 \'df des Kommentars) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 atque omnis ornatus. >Actor<\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [bis hierher gleichlautend mit Frankfurt, StuUB, {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ms. Barth 69}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , 280\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , danach abweichend:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ex quibus liquet et deum vnum et illius cura mundum dirigi ... - post huius vite laboriosum cum virtute decursum assumptus est in celum et sedet ...; >Explicit liber de Consonancia Nature et gratie Editus a Sacre pagine professore Fratre Raphaele de Pornaxio Conuentus Ianuensis ordinis predicatorum<. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [mit anderer Tinte nachgetragen] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 >1445<.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (167\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra-vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 >Tabula ad inueniendum quo capitulo posita sint Euangelia ...<\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; (168\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) alphabetisches Register, \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 >Abstinencia< Abstinencie forma et commendatio ... - >\u167 \'a7< ypocrite et >\u167 \'a7< foris per totum. >Explicit tabula ad librum consonantie nature et gratie M\u176 \'b0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  \u183 \'b7 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 CCCC\u176 \'b0lvij\u176 \'b0 die iiij\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Maj ...<; Pro intellectu huius tabule ... - Et sic de alijs. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Teiledition durch K. MICHEL, Der Liber de consonancia nature et gracie des Raphael von Pornaxio, M\u252 \'fcnster 1915 (Beitr. z. Geschichte d. Philosophie d. Mittelalters 18,1). {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 STEGM\u220 \'dcLLER, RB 5, Nr. 7174}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; KAEPPELI III, S. 296, Nr. 3437; R. CREYTENS, Rapha\u235 \'ebl de Pornassio, AFP 49 (1979), S. 145-192, hier S. 156, 167, 188 (40), ohne diese Hs. 175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb-vb \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 leer.}

